            <ArticleTitle>Where does it hurt? An interdisciplinary approach to improving the quality of pain assessment and management in the neonatal intensive care unit.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>143-59</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Identifying a premature infant's response to noxious stimuli and knowing when it is appropriate to intervene are major issues for the caregiver. After completing a pilot study, the staff of a 42-bed neonatal intensive care unit targeted improved pain assessment and management for further analysis. Using a series of Plan, Do, Check, and Act cycles they designed a stepwise set of interventions that resulted in the improved assessment and management of the neonate in pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
